course: dictionary
lesson: 10747
title: Urban: towns and cities
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Urban means to do with towns and cities, not the countryside. You can spot it in phrases like «urban area», «urban life» and «urban park». When you meet it, ask: is this place a busy town or city?
explain: «Urban foxes live in towns because there is food, shelter and few enemies.» The word urban tells you the foxes live in towns, not in fields or woods. Read the words around it to check.
explain: Rural is the opposite of urban. Rural means to do with the countryside, like farms and villages. A busy city is urban, and a quiet village in the fields is rural.
explain: Watch out for «urban legend». It is a set phrase with its own meaning: a made-up scary story that many people believe but is not true. Learn it as one phrase, because the whole phrase is what matters.
fact: Urban means to do with towns and cities, not the countryside.
fact: The opposite of urban is rural, which means to do with the countryside.
fact: «Urban areas» are the parts of a country where towns and cities are.
fact: Cairo, Lagos and Kinshasa are among Africa's largest cities, each with well over 15 million people in their wider urban areas.
fact: An «urban legend» is a made-up scary story that spreads as if it were true, and knowing it was invented helps the fear fade.
exercise: «Urban foxes live in towns because there is food, shelter and few enemies.» Where do urban foxes live? | Under the sea | *In towns | In the desert | In deep forests
exercise: What does urban mean? | Old and broken | *To do with towns and cities | Wild and empty | To do with the countryside and farms
exercise: «The story of the man with a hook for a hand is an urban legend.» What is an urban legend? | *A made-up scary story that spreads as if it were true | A fact book about towns | A true story from history | A map of a city
test: Which word means the opposite of urban? | *Rural | Crowded | Modern | Busy
test: «Cairo, Lagos and Kinshasa are Africa's largest cities, each with well over 15 million people in their wider urban areas.» Which word means to do with towns and cities? | Wild | *Urban | Ancient | Rural
exam: Jayden says urban means to do with the countryside. Is he right? | Yes, urban means wild woods | Yes, urban means fields and farms | No, urban means very old | *No, urban means to do with towns and cities
